<!--
  §4.2.4.1 cache-staleness `_NEG` body: the lwIP ingress-fault self-validation of
  the positive `dut_arp_request_after_*` guards (ARP_04/06/32/33/34/35).

  The positive TEACHES the DUT an address and then provokes an egress to it, so a
  conformant DUT never needs to resolve: any opcode-1 ARP Request it emits means the
  teaching did not take, and that is the positive's fail final. Its `_NEG` arms
  kArpFaultIgnoreLearn, whose netif input hook swallows the teaching Request before
  lwIP's etharp sees it, so the address is never held.

    Pass:    an opcode-1 ARP Request from the DUT's own MAC — the resolution the
             positive forbids, present here because the fault took.
    Fail:    deadline_exceeded -> fail_compliant — no such Request within the
             window: the DUT resolved from cache anyway, so the flavor never
             reached the teaching frame (a wiring regression, NOT a DUT
             conformance violation; role fault_injection_inert).

  WHY THIS ONE MAY KEY ON A DUT ARP REQUEST when arp_group_c_drop_and_emit_neg may
  not. There the cache is deliberately never populated, so the DUT ARP-resolves the
  tester for its own UT control-plane ACKs and that conformant Request is
  indistinguishable from the behaviour under test. Here the teaching is what a
  conformant run relies on: with it intact the DUT has no reason to emit ANY
  Request, control plane included, which is why the positive passes on this fixture
  today. The discriminator is sound precisely because the teaching is part of the
  premise rather than withheld from it.

  Param-less, shared by the cluster. 5 s deadline matches the §4.2 `_NEG` cases.
-->
<sce:template xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
              xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
              name="arp_cache_staleness_neg">

  <sce:context id="captured"
               cpp:type="tc8::ArpCaptured"
               cpp:include="sce_integration/arp_captured.h"/>

  <sce:context id="expected"
               cpp:type="tc8::ArpExpected"
               cpp:include="sce_integration/arp_expected.h"/>

  <state id="listening">
    <onentry>
      <send event="deadline_exceeded" delay="5s"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="arp_observed"
                cond="cpp:captured.opcode == 1 and captured.sender_hw == expected.dut_iface_mac"
                target="pass"/>
    <transition event="deadline_exceeded" target="fail_compliant"/>
  </state>

  <final id="pass">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"pass"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>

  <final id="fail_compliant">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"fail","reason":"dut_resolved_from_cache_despite_ignore_learn_flavor","role":"fault_injection_inert"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</sce:template>
